course: dictionary
lesson: 2625
title: Deserve: getting what is fair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To deserve something means you should get it because of what you have done or what you are like. «You worked hard, you deserve a break.» The hard work is the reason, so the break is fair. When you meet deserve, ask yourself: why should this person get it?
explain: Deserve can be used for good things, like a reward, or for bad things, like a punishment. In sport, «they deserved to win» means they played better than the other team. In stories, the greedy villain gets caught and the kind hero is rewarded, so they get what they deserve.
explain: In everyday life, deserve often means fairness. «Everyone deserves to be treated kindly and fairly, however they look.» Here it means every person has a right to kindness, whatever they look like. «Everyone deserves some private space, so ask siblings calmly to knock.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The words that come before and after deserve tell you whether the thing is good or bad, and why it is deserved. Then try your meaning in the sentence: does «should get, because of what they did» still fit?
fact: Deserve means you should get something because of what you have done or what you are like.
fact: Deserve can be used for good things, such as a reward, or bad things, such as a punishment.
fact: «Deserved» can mean that someone played better, as in «they deserved to win».
fact: Deserve is a verb: deserve, deserves, deserved, deserving.
fact: «Everyone deserves respect and kindness, whatever they look like.»
exercise: «You worked hard all week, so you deserve a break.» What does deserve mean here? | You have lost your break | *You should get a break because of your hard work | You are too tired to rest | You must go to bed early
exercise: In many stories, the greedy villain is caught. Which character usually gets what they deserve? | The bird in the tree | The narrator | The kind hero, who is rewarded | *The greedy villain, who is caught
exercise: «Everyone deserves some private space, so ask siblings calmly to knock.» What does deserves mean in this sentence? | Keeps it hidden from others | *Has a right to get it, so it should be given | Is able to give it away | Asks for it loudly
test: «The other team played much better, so they deserved to win.» What does deserved mean? | They wanted to win very much | They lost the match | *They should win because they played better | They were lucky to win
test: Which words in «Everyone deserves to be treated kindly and fairly, however they look.» show that looks do not change what people should get? | fairly | treated | kindly | *however they look
exam: What is the best meaning of deserve? | *You should get something because of what you have done or what you are like | You are sure to lose | You must give something away | You have to pay for something
